The request to find the workplace policy document in your SharePoint site cannot be completed directly at this moment because I do not have direct, active access to search your organization's Microsoft SharePoint environment.
To search, view, and manage your SharePoint files natively through me, your Google Cloud administrator needs to first set up the **Microsoft SharePoint Online connector** in Gemini Enterprise.
---
### 📌 Recommended Action: Connect SharePoint to Gemini Enterprise
Good call looking to access your policies directly here! To enable this capability, please share the following instructions with your workspace or Google Cloud administrator. Once the connector is configured, I will be able to search and retrieve any workplace policy document on your SharePoint sites.
#### Step 1: Register Gemini Enterprise in Microsoft Entra ID
Before starting in Google Cloud, your administrator must register Gemini Enterprise as an authorized application:
1. Sign in to the **Microsoft Entra admin center** and go to **Identity > Applications > App registrations**.
2. Click **New registration** and configure:
   * **Name**: Enter a name (e.g., `Gemini Enterprise SharePoint`).
   * **Supported account types**: Select **Accounts in this organizational directory only** (Single tenant).
   * **Redirect URI**: Choose **Web** and enter:
     `https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/console/oauth/sharepoint_oauth.html`
3. Click **Register**, then go to the **Authentication** tab and add a second redirect URI:
   `https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/oauth-redirect`
4. Go to **Certificates & secrets**, create a **New client secret**, and copy the secret **Value** (you will also need the **Application (client) ID** and **Tenant ID** from the App Overview page).
#### Step 2: Grant the Required API Permissions
In your Entra ID app registration, click **API permissions** > **Add a permission** to grant the following Delegated permissions (which ensure I only find files that the signed-in user actually has access to):
| API Category | Required Permission | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Microsoft SharePoint** | `Sites.Search.All` (Delegated) | Allows running search queries on behalf of the signed-in user. |
| **Microsoft SharePoint** | `AllSites.Read` (Delegated) | Allows reading documents and list items the user has access to. |
| **Microsoft Graph (Optional)** | `Sites.ReadWrite.All`, `Files.ReadWrite` | Enable if you want to allow me to upload, move, or edit documents. |
*Make sure your administrator clicks **Grant admin consent** after adding the permissions.*
#### Step 3: Create the SharePoint Data Store in Google Cloud
1. Go to the **Google Cloud console** and navigate to **Gemini Enterprise > Data stores**.
2. Click **Create data store** and select **Microsoft SharePoint** as the source.
3. Select **Federated search** (queries SharePoint in real-time) or **Data ingestion** (indexes files directly for deeper content search), then click **Continue**.
4. Provide the **Client ID**, **Client Secret**, **Tenant ID**, and your SharePoint **Instance URI** (e.g., `https://{your-domain}.sharepoint.com`).
5. Click **Login** to authorize the connection and complete the setup.
---
### 💡 Alternative Ways to Find the Document Now
While the connector is being set up, you can manually locate your policy document using these steps:
* **Check SharePoint Directly**: Navigate to your company's SharePoint home portal and search for terms like `workplace policy`, `employee handbook`, `safety guidelines`, or `HR policies` in the top search bar.
* **Look in Local Downloads or Synced Drives**: If you have previously synced SharePoint libraries to your computer, check your local **OneDrive - [Company Name]** folders in your file explorer.
